1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,640
 Hi, and welcome to this course. I am so excited to have you here, and I want to make sure you get the most value out of this course

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,400
 The course is divided into two sections

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:18,160
 Section 1 takes you from not knowing anything about MCP to building your first MCP server in Python

4
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:25,000
 If everyone at work is talking about MCP, but you have no idea what it is then this section is for you

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:34,920
 You will learn how to connect LLM to external applications and API and then you will be using cloud disktop to connect to your MCP server

6
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:37,200
 Once you finish off with the foundation

7
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:44,520
 Section 2 shifts your mindset to a security engineer or penetration tester or even a software engineer

8
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:53,200
 You will start seeing MCP servers as targets to attacks. We will exploit the most common vulnerabilities in MCP servers

9
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:59,880
 And you will learn how to attack MCP servers prompt injection in a chatbot application and much more

10
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:05,760
 If you are already familiar with MCP and you have built local and remote MCP servers before

11
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:10,480
 Then you can immediately skip section 1 and jump immediately to section 2

12
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:17,040
 However, I still recommend you to at least skim through section 1 to ensure you have the right foundation

13
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:22,200
 I wish I had a course like this when I started my journey in learning MCP

14
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:29,600
 So I am so excited to share my knowledge with you. Alright, let's get started and I will see you in the next lecture. Thanks for watching

